# Production build config for the public PWA.
#
# These are the *publishable* client keys: they are designed to be public and
# ship inside the visible JavaScript bundle on every deployment, so committing
# them exposes nothing a visitor cannot already read. Row-level security in
# supabase/schema.sql is what protects the data.
#
# The secret service-role key must NEVER appear here or anywhere in this repo.
#
# Precedence: real environment variables beat .env files in Vite, so if
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL / VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are ever set as repository or
# environment secrets in GitHub Actions, those values win over this file.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://vaptlqzdqqaccdbtctya.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_lfjxhTGFCxUwvDNGNJ5ERg_jDZk5ww_
